#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""apple-plugin-health - daily Health totals and workouts, from files the iPhone writes.

🛑 THERE IS NO HEALTH DATA ON A MAC. HealthKit links on macOS and refuses
every call, no signing or entitlement changes that, and no local store
exists (docs/apple-health.md, measured). So this plugin reads no Apple
store: it reads two kinds of file that the iPhone puts in iCloud Drive, and
keeps what it read in its own SQLite store so a day is never parsed twice.

  the daily file    written by the "Apple Tools Health Export" shortcut
                    (plugins/health/build-shortcut.py): one line per day
                    per type, Health's own totals, for the last few days.
                    The user runs it on the phone; the Mac cannot.
  the export        Health app → profile → Export All Health Data →
                    export.zip. Every record ever, and the WORKOUTS, which
                    no shortcut can read. `apple health import export.zip`.

It makes no connection, needs no grant and reads nothing outside the
configured folders and the files named on its command line.

    apple plugins enable health
    apple health import ~/Downloads/export.zip     # once, the history
    apple health sync                              # read new daily files
    apple health days --since 14
    apple health workouts --since 90 --json
    apple health shortcut --to ~/Downloads         # the file to install

`index` is what apple-index calls: it syncs, then emits one record per day
and one per workout. A raw sample — one heart-rate reading — is not a
document and is never indexed, the same rule Dawarich's GPS points follow.
"""
